const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"收益率曲线与持有期收益不同",en:"Yields are not holding-period returns"},body:{zh:"Cochrane与Piazzesi研究债券预期超额收益如何随时间变化。研究对象是未来一年持有债券的超额收益，而不是今天的到期收益率或一年后的短期利率；三者不能互相替代。",en:"Cochrane and Piazzesi study time variation in expected excess bond returns. Their target is a one-year holding-period excess return, not today's yield or next year's short rate."}},{title:{zh:"持有一年后，债券期限也变短一年",en:"A year of holding also shortens maturity"},body:{zh:"原文使用Fama–Bliss一至五年零息债券价格。买入一只n年债券，一年后卖出时它已是n−1年债券；持有期对数收益再减去期初一年期利率，才得到这里的超额收益。用同一期限收益率的年度变化代替，会漏掉滚动期限与价格转换。",en:"The paper uses Fama–Bliss zero-coupon prices for one- through five-year maturities. An n-year bond becomes an n−1-year bond when sold one year later; its log holding return is then reduced by the initial one-year rate. A change in a constant-maturity yield is not that return calculation."},reference:{url:"https://web.stanford.edu/~piazzesi/cp.pdf",label:{zh:"原文第I.A–I.B节：定义与零息价格",en:"Original §§I.A–I.B: definitions and zero-coupon prices"}}},{title:{zh:"从期初远期利率提取信息",en:"Use information available initially"},body:{zh:"作者将一年超额收益与期初一组远期利率联系起来，发现一个帐篷形线性组合能概括多个期限的预测关系。这里的组合是统计表示，不是本站提供的交易信号，也不是任意挑选几个期限即可重建。",en:"Regressions relate one-year excess returns to initial forward rates. A tent-shaped combination summarizes relationships across maturities. It is a statistical representation, not a site-provided trading signal or an arbitrary choice of tenors."}},{title:{zh:"拟合曲线的因子未必保留全部信息",en:"Curve factors may omit information"},body:{zh:"论文强调，预测收益的信息有一部分不同于描述收益率曲线主要变化的水平、斜率和曲率。一个模型很好地拟合了收益率，不代表它自动保留了另一个目标所需要的全部信息。",en:"Some return-forecasting information differs from level, slope and curvature movements explaining most yield variation. A good fit for yields need not preserve everything relevant to a different target."}},{title:{zh:"月度观测的一年收益会重叠",en:"Monthly observations of annual returns overlap"},body:{zh:"每个月向前看一年，相邻观测会共享大部分持有月份，因此样本行数不能当作独立年度实验次数。第I.C节专门比较重叠收益下的统计处理。作者也用滞后的远期利率检查共用价格测量误差；这与简单增加观测数量是不同的稳健性问题。",en:"Rolling a one-year horizon forward monthly makes adjacent observations share most holding months. Row count is therefore not a count of independent annual experiments. Section I.C examines overlapping-return inference, while lagged forward rates address shared-price measurement error. These are distinct checks, not benefits obtained merely by adding rows."},reference:{url:"https://web.stanford.edu/~piazzesi/cp.pdf",label:{zh:"原文第I.C节及引言：重叠窗口与测量误差",en:"Original §I.C and introduction: overlap and measurement error"}}},{title:{zh:"与前两篇形成三个层次",en:"Three questions in one sequence"},body:{zh:"Nelson–Siegel关注曲线形状，Diebold–Li关注曲线动态，这篇关注持有期超额收益。本站建议分别保存价格、收益率、远期利率和期限约定；不要把供应商同名字段当作论文定义，也不要把样本内关系写成当前可用预测。",en:"Nelson–Siegel addresses shape, Diebold–Li dynamics, and this paper holding-period excess returns. Preserve prices, yields, forwards and tenor conventions separately; vendor labels alone do not establish equivalence to the paper's inputs."}}],readerLimits:{zh:"美国国债历史样本的统计关系不保证当前或跨市场预测；持有期重叠、利率测量和样本外检验仍影响解释。",en:"Historical US Treasury relationships do not guarantee current or cross-market forecasts; overlapping horizons, rate measurement and out-of-sample tests matter."}};export{e as default};
